# Logs
*.log

# Environment
.env
.env.backup
.env.production

# Timestamped .env backups.
#
# `env.bak-*` is deliberately explicit rather than a broad `*.bak` rule: a
# blanket pattern would also swallow backups of files that are safe to keep.
# These copies contain every secret in .env — DB credentials, API keys — and
# the naming is produced by `Copy-Item .env ".env.bak-<timestamp>"`, so the
# wildcard is what actually matches what gets created.
.env.bak-*
.env.bak.*

